{
 "_note": "<multiselect> and <tagsfield> as pure folds, plus the ACCESSIBILITY ANNOUNCEMENTS all three renderers must speak identically (00-conventions §8: accessibility is contract). MULTISELECT: toggling an already-selected value removes it; adding at `max` is refused with reason 'max-reached' and changed:false — never a silent drop of the oldest. Selection order is INSERTION order. TAGS: the committed text is split on every character of `separator` (default ','), each part is trimmed, empty parts vanish, a duplicate is refused ('duplicate'), a part failing the `validate` pattern is refused ('invalid'), and once `max` is reached every further part is refused ('max-reached') — the refusals are RETURNED, not swallowed, so on:add can report them. BACKSPACE on an EMPTY query removes the last chip and returns it (the interaction everyone expects and nobody implements); backspace with a non-empty query removes nothing.",
